1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,434
This whole chapter turns on one question.

2
00:00:02,434 --> 00:00:03,697
Does the order matter?

3
00:00:03,697 --> 00:00:07,773
If it does, you are counting arrangements: permutations.

4
00:00:07,773 --> 00:00:11,614
If it does not, you are counting selections: combinations.

5
00:00:11,614 --> 00:00:17,122
Get that decision right, and every exam question becomes a short calculation.

